The recent discussion about genociding nymphs made me wonder what
people think of creatures' usefulness.  Many of the "nasty" (depending
on your preference) creatures have very nice side-effects too.  I
tried to make a list, but couldn't fill some of the fields.

(obviously spoilers follow)



monster name    why annoying?           special effects
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
mind flayer     eats my mind            corpse can be "brain food"
cockatrice      petrifies me            corpse will be great weapon
;               drowns me               ?
L               spell casting etc.      ?
wraith          level drain             eat corpse to gain level
V               level drain             ?
D               very strong             intrinsics, DSM
gremlin         steals intrinsic        might steal that annoying intrinsic
n               steals stuff            source of ( and ! for polypiling
rust monster    rusts metal things      eats chain of punishment
rock mole       messes up map           ditto
U               ditto                   \ these two are wimpy enough and
dwarves         ditto                   /  I don't really care about map
titan           spell, summon friends   ?
gelatinous cube slurps my BoH           ?

The others I've seen people genocide are mumakil and grid bugs, but I
don't think they deserve to be on this list. :)

I guess this pretty much sums up why I like to genocide ;, L, V and g.
Mind flayers won't be too much of a problem if you have a helmet and a
blessed unicorn horn (why the heck are you that deep in the dungeon if
you don't have these?), cockatrices if you have lizard corpses, rust
monsters if you have already rustproofed your stuff, nymphs if you
have a weapon string enough to kill them in one or two turns (e.g.,
Mjollnir).  Gremlins also won't be a problem if you don't play at
night. :)

